body:
As observed in the PR (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114459), the C# bindings generator always uses `int` for integers as the element type of TypedArrays. Fixing this would likely break compatibility with a lot of other methods, but we could still only apply the fix to specific methods like `GetOrphanNodeIds`. A previous attempt to fix this was made in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/95492, I'll try to revive the conversation.

For now, one could workaround this by casting the `Array<int>` to an untyped `Array`, and then casting the `Variant` to `ulong` like this:

```csharp
Array<int> orphanIds = GetOrphanIds();
Array orphanIdsUntyped = (Array)orphanIds;
Variant orphanIdVariant = orphanIdsUntyped[0];
ulong orphanId = orphanIdVariant.As<ulong>();
```

Also, this is technically a duplicate of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113248, but I'll keep it open because it's a much more concrete ask. And, while we may not apply the fix generally, we may still apply it in specific cases such as this one. So, I want to keep this open to track one specific API that should be considered for fixing.
